# UI/UX Layout Standards

When developing or modifying Page UIs in this project, enforce the following structural consistency rules:

1. **Skeleton Loaders over Spinners:** 
    For data-fetching "loading" states, always replace simple spinners (e.g. `<Loader2/>`) with structural `<Skeleton/>` grids that mimic the upcoming content blocks. This completely eradicates layout jarring when the page initially drops into existence.

2. **Full-width Flexibility:**
    Always assure parent flex-column layout containers use explicit `w-full`. If a flex item contains only tiny sized skeletons, it will shrink-wrap into the center of the viewport, which ruins the perceived skeleton loading illusion. Explicit `w-full` enforces the edges immediately.
    *(e.g. `<div className="w-full flex-1 max-w-[1200px] mx-auto p-8">`)*

3. **Empty States Baseline Heights:**
    Implement empty states (like `cards.length === 0`) with explicitly defined `min-h-[400px]` constraints instead of fixed vertical dimensions that shift surrounding elements upwards. Maintain layout stability even when empty.
